  "worked_solution": "We must bring all variables to one side of the equation and all constants to the other side. \n\nNotice that we have $-3t$ on the left-hand side and $3t$ on the right-hand side. Since the variable on the right-hand side has a larger coefficient, let's bring all the variables to this side.\n\nThe first step is to remove the $-3t$ from the left-hand side of the equation. We do this by adding $3t$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4-3t & =3t-2 \\\\ -4-3t+3t & =3t-2+3t \\\\ -4 & =6t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we remove the $-2$ from the right-hand side. We do this by adding $2$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =6t-2 \\\\ -4+2 & =6t-2+2 \\\\ -2 & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide both sides of the equation by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =6t \\\\ \\frac{(-2)}{6} & =\\frac{6t}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\cancel{6}t}{\\cancel{6}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & =t \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
